  "title": "# Banner boilerplates pack (Urgent, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"Build me a shitload of new ban…",
  "asked": "# Banner boilerplates pack (Urgent, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"Build me a shitload of new banners, a whole bunch of them. I want some boilerplates.\" He wants many ready-made starter banners (boilerplates) he can pick, then edit in the new banner editor. A sibling build `banner-editor` (branch claude/banner-editor, may not be pushed yet) is building the banner editor right now: long-press / right-click > Edit banner, drag-and-drop snapping widgets, remove/add widgets, saved through the axHub appearance document. Start with steps 1 and 3 (they only need the existing banner asset type). Before step 2, `git fetch origin claude/banner-editor` and merge it if it exists, so the picker lives in its editor; if it still isn't there, put the picker in Settings > Appearance and leave a hook the editor can call. Don't duplicate the editor. Do: 1. At least 20 boilerplate banners as hot-swappable assets (the existing banner asset type), each a different, useful arrangement of the existing banner widgets: e.g. minimal, developer (builds, approvals, push), ops (VPS health, alerts), voice-first (Amber/mic), dashboard-dense, phone-compact, presenter/clean, focus, notifications-first, search-first, etc. Every one passes the asset validators, works at 412 wide and desktop, and uses tokens only. 2. A picker: a gallery of the boilerplates with a live preview; pick one to apply, then tweak in the editor. Saving goes through axHub so every app follows. 3. Ship them with every app (shared assets) so the hub look can name any of them. 4. Tests / asset checks, check-theme, check-controls, help pack, UI Review desktop + phone shots of the gallery and several banners (--group \"banner-pack - <Mon D h:mm AM/PM>\"). Brett started to add \"and when I click...\" but was cut off: leave a THREADS note that this part is still to be asked. Rules: one session, no sub-agents. Tokens only (--fx-*), framework controls, no var() fallbacks. Patches paused. Add a THREADS.md row (profile urgent) and update each step. Commit + push branch claude/banner-pack often; open the PR at the end (push banner merges it); merge origin/main (and banner-editor if its PR merged) before the PR. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
